            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Penrose-Hawking Singularity Theorems</strong><br>\nThe Penrose-Hawking Singularity Theorems show that singularities, such as those at the center of black holes, are not just theoretical constructs but can exist in reality. This work also suggests that there was a singularity at the beginning of the universe, lending weight to the Big Bang theory.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Twistor Theory</strong><br>\nPenrose introduced twistor theory, which has provided a new perspective on the nature of space and time. Twistor theory is a mathematical framework that combines geometric and quantum ideas in a novel way, potentially offering a path to reconcile general relativity with quantum physics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Penrose's Books and Public Outreach</strong><br>\nPenrose has authored several books aimed at both scientists and the general public. His works discuss the laws of nature, the role of consciousness in physics, and the possibility of artificial intelligence. His books, such as \"The Emperor's New Mind\" and \"Shadows of the Mind,\" have stimulated public interest in science.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
